            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "numericInput",
              "title": "Priya's interest income",
              "prompt": "From Priya's worksheet: ICICI FD interest ₹62,000, SBI FD interest ₹38,000, Kotak savings interest ₹4,300 and interest on refund ₹552. What total interest income should she report?",
              "correctValue": 104852,
              "tolerance": 0,
              "unit": "₹",
              "explanation": "₹62,000 + ₹38,000 + ₹4,300 + ₹552 = ₹1,04,852. Note that the SFT-016 entry for ICICI is a duplicate of the TDS-194A entry, so the ₹62,000 is counted once.",
              "_key": "k105"
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "numericInput",
              "title": "Total credits",
              "prompt": "Gautam's reconciliation shows salary TDS of ₹1,12,000, bank TDS of ₹3,400, TCS of ₹15,000 on a foreign remittance and advance tax of ₹20,000 paid in March 2026. What total tax credit should he claim?",
              "correctValue": 150400,
              "tolerance": 0,
              "unit": "₹",
              "explanation": "₹1,12,000 + ₹3,400 + ₹15,000 + ₹20,000 = ₹1,50,400. The TDS and TCS appear in Form 26AS. The advance tax appears in AIS under payment of taxes.",
              "_key": "k106"
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "quiz",
              "title": "Classify the difference",
              "question": "Rekha's AIS shows SFT-017 sales of listed shares worth ₹5,60,000. Her broker's tax P&L shows a short-term gain of ₹42,000 on those sales. What kind of difference is this?",
              "options": [
                "Income she forgot, so she must report ₹5,60,000",
                "Sale value, not income, so she reports the ₹42,000 gain",
                "A duplicate she should give feedback on",
                "An entry that is not hers"
              ],
              "correctIndex": 1,
              "explanation": "SFT-017 shows the sale value. What is taxable is the gain after deducting cost, which her broker's tax P&L shows as ₹42,000. No feedback is needed if the sales are correct.",
              "_key": "k107"
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "fillInTheBlank",
              "title": "Which year for which document?",
              "textWithBlank": "When reconciling income for FY 2025-26, you select FY 2025-26 in AIS but assessment year ___ in Form 26AS.",
              "correctAnswers": [
                "2026-27",
                "AY 2026-27",
                "2026-2027"
              ],
              "explanation": "AIS works on the financial year. Form 26AS on TRACES works on the assessment year, which is the financial year plus one.",
              "_key": "k108"
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "scenario",
              "title": "Joseph's three differences",
              "scenario": "Joseph, a lecturer in Thiruvananthapuram, reconciles his FY 2025-26 documents and finds: (1) his Form 16 and Form 26AS both show salary TDS of ₹68,000, but AIS salary shows ₹9,60,000 while Form 16 Part B shows gross salary of ₹9,60,000 and taxable salary of ₹7,85,000; (2) AIS shows ₹2,150 of interest from a post office savings account he forgot; (3) AIS shows a ₹1,50,000 SFT-018 redemption twice, and TIS shows ₹3,00,000.",
              "prompt": "Classify each difference and say what Joseph should do.",
              "modelAnswer": "(1) Not an error. AIS shows gross salary, which matches Form 16 Part B. The ₹7,85,000 is after exemptions and deductions, which he claims in his return. No action needed. (2) Income he forgot. He should report the ₹2,150 as interest income, and under the old regime he may claim the savings interest deduction against it. (3) Duplicate reporting that TIS did not remove. He should give feedback marking the second entry as duplicate, check that TIS drops to ₹1,50,000, and then compute the capital gain on that single redemption from his CAMS or KFintech statement.",
              "_key": "k109"
            },
            {
