            {
              "_type": "keyTakeaways",
              "points": [
                "Reconcile both ways: everything the department knows should be in your return, and every claim should be in the department's records.",
                "Match salary and salary TDS across Form 16, Form 26AS and AIS for each employer.",
                "Go through every SFT entry in AIS. Forgotten interest and dividends are the most common misses.",
                "Classify differences before acting: forgotten income, duplicate, sale value, gross amount, timing, not yours or missing credit.",
                "Claim only the TDS and TCS shown in Form 26AS, plus challans shown in AIS.",
                "Report exempt income such as long-term gains within the exemption limit. Do not leave it out."
